pr.body:
Fixes issue #233 by enabling support for variable interpolation into the `env` struct tag.

```go
type cli struct {
	EnvFlag string `env:"${myEnv}" help:"Looks at ${myEnv}"`
}

ctx := kong.Parse(&cli{}, kong.Vars{
	"myEnv": "AN_ENV_VAR",
})
```

linkedIssues.body:
I noticed that `kong.Var` interpolation does not support the `env` tag. I would like to be able to interpolate the environment variable name itself, since in my use case these are defined elsewhere in other packages and I'd rather not hardcode it.

If there's some other preferred solution to this using existing functionality, I'd be okay with that (assuming I don't have to add dozens of lines of code to do so).

```go
import (
	"fmt"
	"os"
	"github.com/alecthomas/kong"
)

const SomeEnvVar = "SOME_ENV_VAR"

type cli struct {
	MyEnv string `env:"${myEnv}" help:"An environment variable"`
}

// Set environment variable
if err := os.Setenv(SomeEnvVar, "something/or/other"); err != nil {
	panic(err)
}

cli := cli{}
ctx := kong.Parse(&cli, kong.Vars{
	"myEnv": SomeEnvVar,
})

// Does not interpolate to "something/or/other" (is empty string)
fmt.Printf("cli.MyEnv = %s\n", cli.MyEnv)
```

